prologue.caption01 = Once, this land was green from one horizon to the other. We were the Ancients, and our cities shone with light.
prologue.caption02 = Our golems hauled the stone and tended the forges. They never tired, and we wanted for nothing.
prologue.caption03 = And the Great Portal stood open. Caravans travelled between the worlds, and nothing seemed out of reach.
prologue.caption04 = But the more we had, the more we feared to lose it. Our rulers watched each other, and none of them slept.
prologue.caption05 = Then one of them panicked and gave the order. The others answered within the hour, and our golems marched to war.
prologue.caption06 = None of them wanted to lose, so all of us did. What took centuries to build burned in a single night.
prologue.caption07 = Those who could fled through the portals into other worlds. Perhaps their children still remember the way back.
prologue.caption08 = Then the Great Portal flickered and went dark. And with it, the world we knew.
prologue.caption09 = I stayed behind. When the sirens fell silent, I sealed the bunker behind me.
prologue.caption10 = We had air, water and the capsules. I kept a handful of seeds, lay down in the cold and waited.
prologue.caption11 = Centuries passed. Grass grew over the ruins, and the land forgot we had ever been here.
prologue.caption12 = Until, one day, the last of the power ran out …
